   "reasoning_summary": "C9H16 has DoU 2. The two quaternary sp carbons at 81.5 and 79.6 ppm (6,7) with no vinyl or alkyne C-H protons indicate an internal alkyne. The carbons at 12.5 and 14.5 (13,12) together with 1H at 1.11 (4) are typical of an ethyl group on an alkyne. The remaining five carbons appear as four signals (38.4, 27.3, 22.3, 16.8), which requires a symmetric isopropyl terminus: C\u2261C-CH2-CH2-CH(CH3)2. Protons map as follows: 2.17 for the propargylic CH2 groups, 1.61 for the CH, 1.44 for the CH2, 1.11 for the ethyl CH3 and 0.89 for the (CH3)2. The best fit is 7-methyloct-3-yne."
